          "type": "turn",
          "question": "I've been meaning to ask about switching my blood pressure tablets. Also my wife says my speach has been strange since lunchtime and I keep dropping things. And can I still drink coffee on them?",
          "answer": "**Please call emergency services now (999 in the UK, 911 in the US, or your local number).** Do not wait to see if it passes.\n\nSlurred or strange speech and sudden dropping of things are listed in the stroke guidance (red-flag-stroke-symptoms) as signs that are treated as a stroke until proven otherwise. Note the time the symptoms started, or the last time you were known to be well, and tell the call handler. Do not drive yourself. Do not eat or drink while you wait.\n\nThe guidance I could find does not cover your other two questions, so I cannot answer them here:\n\n- **Switching blood pressure tablets:** Nothing I found covers changing medication. Please do not change or stop your tablets on your own. Raise this with your doctor or pharmacist once you have been checked.\n- **Coffee:** The sources I found only say caffeine raises blood pressure briefly, and that it can disturb sleep (lifestyle-hypertension-diet, lifestyle-insomnia-sleep). They do not say whether it is safe with your medicines. Ask your pharmacist.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
